//! The `dropsetinfo` rows the `[Dispatch]` `Pouches` and `Breakables` levers
//! multiply, by dropset key, on Crimson Desert build 26361232.
//!
//! Generated by crates/tools/src/bin/gen-dropsets.rs (`just gen-dropsets`) from
//! the game's own archive tables, every record walked to its last byte:
//! dropsetinfo, gimmickinfo, interactioninfo, breakableobjectinfo,
//! itemuseinfo, iteminfo, multichangeinfo, missioninfo and factionnode. Do
//! not edit by hand; rerun `just gen-dropsets`.
//!
//! - `Pouch`: 88 rows. The dropset of an `itemuseinfo` RandomBox record
//!   (kind 2) an item's `_itemUseInfoList` names: what an item pays when it
//!   is opened (122 items, 122 rows before refusals). The five coin pouches,
//!   and the seed packs, chest items, recipe and gear boxes that open the
//!   same way.
//! - `Breakable`: 15 rows. The `dropSetInfoList` of the 172 gimmick records the
//!   container catalogue calls "Breakable container" (21 rows before refusals):
//!   breakable, a loot list, no loot interaction; barrels, crates, pots, sacks.
//!
//! **Refused: 34 pouch and 6 breakable rows**, each listed in [`REFUSED`] with why.
//! A row another source also pays from (another gimmick class, an interaction
//! or override, a gimmick's productData, crafting, a quest or mission, a
//! dispatch operation, faction research, a religion block cost, or the other
//! group) is refused because multiplying it would multiply that source too; a
//! row with no item entry (knowledge, mounts, pets) has nothing to multiply. The
//! sources the generator does not walk - the character tables' loot and pockets,
//! quest dialogue, stage, sub-level and mini-game rewards - were checked against
//! the catalogue database (`analysis/catalog_db.py`, view `item_source`) on
//! 26361232 and shared none of these rows; repeat that query after an update.
//!
//! Each row carries what the plugin checks the parsed row against before it
//! writes: the record index the manager files it under (the archive header's
//! order), the declared entry count, and `sum(min + max)` over its item
//! entries (kind 0), the only entries either lever multiplies.

/// Which lever a row belongs to.
#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]
pub enum RowGroup {
    /// What an item pays when it is opened: `[Dispatch] Pouches`.
    Pouch,
    /// What a barrel, crate, pot or sack pays when it is smashed:
    /// `[Dispatch] Breakables`.
    Breakable,
}

impl RowGroup {
    /// The word the log lines use.
    pub fn name(self) -> &'static str {
        match self {
            RowGroup::Pouch => "pouch",
            RowGroup::Breakable => "breakable",
        }
    }
}

/// One row.
#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]
pub struct DropsetRow {
    /// The `dropsetinfo` key.
    pub key: u32,
    /// The record index: the row's position in the archive header, which is
    /// the manager's `+0x58` slot the parsed row is filed under.
    pub index: u16,
    pub group: RowGroup,
    /// The declared entry count, the parsed row's `+0x28`.
    pub entries: u16,
    /// `sum(min + max)` over the item (kind 0) entries, vanilla.
    pub item_amounts: i64,
}

/// The game build these rows were generated on.
pub const BUILD: &str = "26361232";

